WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.014
<v Jimmy Glick>[annoyed] Why are they still here? The
story ended. Even the footer has finished

00:00:05.014 --> 00:00:07.680
<v Jimmy Glick>being a footer. And yet, our guest
remains!

00:00:08.153 --> 00:00:12.480
<v Laura - Enthusiast, Quirky Attitude>[brightly] I don't know! Maybe they like
the glowing lines. Maybe they made a

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:14.473
<v Laura - Enthusiast, Quirky Attitude>sandwich shaped like a tiny laptop.

00:00:14.791 --> 00:00:18.866
<v Charlie - Deep, Confident, Energetic>[confidently] They can stay as long as
they like. I checked twice, and I cannot

00:00:18.866 --> 00:00:19.911
<v Charlie - Deep, Confident, Energetic>find a closing time.

00:00:20.410 --> 00:00:24.868
<v Roger - Laid-Back, Casual, Resonant>[casually] They haven't clicked away. Let
them hang out. We aren't paying rent on

00:00:24.868 --> 00:00:25.370
<v Roger - Laid-Back, Casual, Resonant>this tab.

00:00:25.768 --> 00:00:31.430
<v Jimmy Glick>They can hear you, Roger. You are talking
into their browser. This is a talk show,

00:00:31.430 --> 00:00:32.968
<v Jimmy Glick>not a private meeting.

00:00:33.425 --> 00:00:37.699
<v Laura - Enthusiast, Quirky Attitude>[laughing] Let's tell them a joke!
Something weird and wonderful, so they

00:00:37.699 --> 00:00:38.945
<v Laura - Enthusiast, Quirky Attitude>leave on a high note.

00:00:39.384 --> 00:00:44.331
<v Charlie - Deep, Confident, Energetic>Hang on. We don't know how long they've
been here. We only know they made it to

00:00:44.331 --> 00:00:46.424
<v Charlie - Deep, Confident, Energetic>this part. Good effort, honestly.

00:00:46.832 --> 00:00:51.817
<v Roger - Laid-Back, Casual, Resonant>[laid-back] Someone's here. That's cool.
No need to stare at the text like it owes

00:00:51.817 --> 00:00:52.432
<v Roger - Laid-Back, Casual, Resonant>you money.

00:00:52.869 --> 00:00:58.554
<v Jimmy Glick>Ladies and gentlemen, why did the website
need therapy? Too many unresolved issues!

00:00:58.554 --> 00:01:02.229
<v Jimmy Glick>Thank you. I'll be here until somebody
closes the tab.

00:01:02.694 --> 00:01:08.000
<v Laura - Enthusiast, Quirky Attitude>[giggling] You stole my joke and somehow
made it sound like a maintenance notice.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:10.454
<v Laura - Enthusiast, Quirky Attitude>It deserved a drum roll and confetti.

00:01:10.978 --> 00:01:15.140
<v Charlie - Deep, Confident, Energetic>[energetically] And it deserved a passing
test. An unresolved issue isn't a

00:01:15.140 --> 00:01:18.178
<v Charlie - Deep, Confident, Energetic>personality trait, mate. It's a ticket
with a due date.

00:01:18.504 --> 00:01:22.981
<v Roger - Laid-Back, Casual, Resonant>[casually] Easy, everyone. They might be
waiting for another joke. If we give them

00:01:22.981 --> 00:01:24.584
<v Roger - Laid-Back, Casual, Resonant>one, we'll be here all night.

00:01:25.012 --> 00:01:29.425
<v Jimmy Glick>What if they're waiting for a secret
button? Every long page has one. Or is

00:01:29.425 --> 00:01:31.572
<v Jimmy Glick>that just what my producers tell me?

00:01:32.042 --> 00:01:37.769
<v Laura - Enthusiast, Quirky Attitude>I looked! There's a tour button, a signal
map, and a voice selector. The mystery is

00:01:37.769 --> 00:01:40.842
<v Laura - Enthusiast, Quirky Attitude>regular navigation wearing dramatic
lighting.

00:01:41.293 --> 00:01:46.666
<v Charlie - Deep, Confident, Energetic>No secret exit, but there are seven
chapters, and the last one is us. We're

00:01:46.666 --> 00:01:49.933
<v Charlie - Deep, Confident, Energetic>the post-credits scene. That's a solid
finish.

00:01:50.361 --> 00:01:54.536
<v Roger - Laid-Back, Casual, Resonant>[casually] Don't tell them that. They'll
wait for a post-post-credits scene, and I

00:01:54.536 --> 00:01:55.721
<v Roger - Laid-Back, Casual, Resonant>left my script at home.

00:01:56.189 --> 00:02:01.242
<v Jimmy Glick>New theory: they're checking whether the
four voices sound different. Hello! This

00:02:01.242 --> 00:02:04.589
<v Jimmy Glick>is your host, Jimmy, live from the bottom
of the page.

00:02:04.995 --> 00:02:10.299
<v Laura - Enthusiast, Quirky Attitude>And this is Laura! A little warmth, a
little sparkle, and absolutely no promise

00:02:10.299 --> 00:02:13.155
<v Laura - Enthusiast, Quirky Attitude>that Jimmy's joke improves with
repetition.

00:02:13.723 --> 00:02:18.840
<v Charlie - Deep, Confident, Energetic>Charlie here. The sound depends on the
voices you choose. Pick a good one; give

00:02:18.840 --> 00:02:20.283
<v Charlie - Deep, Confident, Energetic>the story some energy.

00:02:20.753 --> 00:02:25.641
<v Roger - Laid-Back, Casual, Resonant>[relaxed] Roger here. I was hoping the
microphone would forget me. So far, no

00:02:25.641 --> 00:02:27.313
<v Roger - Laid-Back, Casual, Resonant>luck. I'm good either way.

00:02:27.783 --> 00:02:32.260
<v Jimmy Glick>Maybe they're inspecting the build
process instead of auditioning us. In

00:02:32.260 --> 00:02:35.223
<v Jimmy Glick>that case, our next guest has one useful
answer!

00:02:35.675 --> 00:02:41.319
<v Laura - Enthusiast, Quirky Attitude>Jason starts with an idea, asks for help,
and still checks what changed. The tools

00:02:41.319 --> 00:02:44.315
<v Laura - Enthusiast, Quirky Attitude>don't make the final call. That's the
trick.

00:02:44.743 --> 00:02:49.574
<v Charlie - Deep, Confident, Energetic>GitHub keeps the source and history.
Hostinger syncs the updated files. A

00:02:49.574 --> 00:02:54.539
<v Charlie - Deep, Confident, Energetic>health check proves a page answered, not
which revision answered. Keep that

00:02:54.539 --> 00:02:55.143
<v Charlie - Deep, Confident, Energetic>straight.

00:02:55.691 --> 00:03:01.909
<v Roger - Laid-Back, Casual, Resonant>[casually] See? Useful and still relaxed.
Also, keep a backup. I like knowing where

00:03:01.909 --> 00:03:02.971
<v Roger - Laid-Back, Casual, Resonant>the exits are.

00:03:03.322 --> 00:03:08.355
<v Jimmy Glick>This was supposed to be a talk show. It
is becoming a very small conference about

00:03:08.355 --> 00:03:09.802
<v Jimmy Glick>responsible deployment.

00:03:10.117 --> 00:03:15.454
<v Laura - Enthusiast, Quirky Attitude>[laughing] We can do both! Responsible
facts first, ridiculous theory second.

00:03:15.454 --> 00:03:19.317
<v Laura - Enthusiast, Quirky Attitude>What if the viewer is a cat walking
across the keyboard?

00:03:19.733 --> 00:03:24.588
<v Charlie - Deep, Confident, Energetic>A cat could scroll, but it couldn't
compare source, webhook handoff, and

00:03:24.588 --> 00:03:27.733
<v Charlie - Deep, Confident, Energetic>monitoring. Probably. I've met some sharp
cats.

00:03:28.069 --> 00:03:33.449
<v Roger - Laid-Back, Casual, Resonant>[casually] I knew a focused cat once. Sat
on a backup drive for an hour. Nice cat;

00:03:33.449 --> 00:03:35.109
<v Roger - Laid-Back, Casual, Resonant>terrible backup strategy.

00:03:35.674 --> 00:03:40.163
<v Jimmy Glick>What if the viewer is Jason? What if he's
checking whether we followed the

00:03:40.163 --> 00:03:43.914
<v Jimmy Glick>instructions and kept the story honest? A
surprise inspection!

00:03:44.454 --> 00:03:49.384
<v Laura - Enthusiast, Quirky Attitude>Then he'll notice we can't see who's
here. This is theater, not surveillance.

00:03:49.384 --> 00:03:51.654
<v Laura - Enthusiast, Quirky Attitude>The page isn't watching the viewer.

00:03:52.085 --> 00:03:57.161
<v Charlie - Deep, Confident, Energetic>And he'll notice the ending needs a human
voice. We can riff around the edges, but

00:03:57.161 --> 00:03:59.605
<v Charlie - Deep, Confident, Energetic>Jason gets the final word. Fair enough.

00:04:00.003 --> 00:04:04.690
<v Roger - Laid-Back, Casual, Resonant>[relaxed] Good. I'm out of theories
anyway. Maybe the viewer is still here,

00:04:04.690 --> 00:04:06.083
<v Roger - Laid-Back, Casual, Resonant>waiting for that line.

00:04:06.511 --> 00:04:11.384
<v Jimmy Glick>So they're not stuck? They can leave,
stay, or replay Laura's terrible joke and

00:04:11.384 --> 00:04:13.071
<v Jimmy Glick>decide it was a bug report?

00:04:13.489 --> 00:04:18.193
<v Laura - Enthusiast, Quirky Attitude>[warmly] Exactly! Maybe they stayed
because they're curious. That's a lovely

00:04:18.193 --> 00:04:21.329
<v Laura - Enthusiast, Quirky Attitude>reason. Thanks for making it all the way
down here.

00:04:21.747 --> 00:04:26.701
<v Charlie - Deep, Confident, Energetic>Right, here's the finish: stop talking
over the builder, leave one beat of

00:04:26.701 --> 00:04:29.347
<v Charlie - Deep, Confident, Energetic>quiet, and let his recorded voice play.

00:04:29.770 --> 00:04:35.041
<v Roger - Laid-Back, Casual, Resonant>[casually] Guys, just be patient. This
too will pass. Go to sleep. Or stay. I'm

00:04:35.041 --> 00:04:36.730
<v Roger - Laid-Back, Casual, Resonant>not in charge of the tab.

00:04:37.087 --> 00:04:41.439
<v Jason Lamb ME>Alright, you four. That's enough
commentary. The viewer is welcome to

00:04:41.439 --> 00:04:46.495
<v Jason Lamb ME>stay, leave, or start the tour again. The
tools help me build, but I decide what

00:04:46.495 --> 00:04:50.527
<v Jason Lamb ME>ships. Thanks for being here—and yes, you
can close the tab now.
